<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
    wis_config.xml.template — RTI Web Integration Service config for the mesh-dashboard
    spike (spikes/wis_mesh_dashboard/PLAN.md step 2).

    Modeled on $NDDSHOME/resource/xml/RTI_WEB_INTEGRATION_SERVICE.xml's ShapesDemo
    <web_integration_service> shape (application/domain_participant/subscriber/data_reader
    nesting) and on
    $NDDSHOME/resource/template/rti_workspace/examples/web_integration_service/rest/simple_shapes_demo
    (domain_library + register_type + topic, referenced by the participant via domain_ref).

    The placeholder line below this comment (a single all-caps token, substituted verbatim
    by run_spike.sh's splice step — NOT repeated here literally, so a naive str.replace over
    the whole file can't also match this description of it) is replaced at spike-run time
    with the types block produced by:
        rtiddsgen -convertToXml -d <tmp> router/admin/RouterAdminTypes.idl
    which — verified by hand, 2026-07-21 — emits a flat (no IDL module wrapper) list of
    <enum>/<struct> elements including <struct name="RouterHealth"> with a plain string
    "router" @key member and a "peers_seen" sequence of RouterPeerRef, matching the IDL in
    router/admin/RouterAdminTypes.idl exactly. That whole block (including the outer
    <types> and </types> tags) gets substituted in as-is, unmodified.

    Domain: 1202, the WAN domain fixed in
    config/e2e_presence_fixed_domains.yaml (the "control_wan"/"platform_wan"
    participants both live there — see that file). RouterHealth heartbeats from both
    router_main roles land in this one domain.

    No custom QoS here: PresenceMonitor's health_qos (router/src/core/PresenceMonitor.cxx)
    writes RouterHealth as RELIABLE + TRANSIENT_LOCAL + KEEP_LAST(1) + DEADLINE 2s +
    AUTOMATIC liveliness (3s lease). WIS's default DataReader QoS (BEST_EFFORT, VOLATILE,
    no deadline) is RxO-compatible with that writer (a reader may always request less than
    what's offered), so nothing needs to be added here for the match to succeed.
-->
<dds xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="/home/rti/rti_connext_dds-7.7.0/resource/schema/rti_web_integration_service.xsd">

    __ROUTER_ADMIN_TYPES__

    <domain_library name="RouterAdminDomainLibrary">
        <domain name="MeshWanDomain" domain_id="1202">
            <!-- register_type's own "name" lives in the same per-domain XML-DOM
                 namespace as topic's "name", so giving both "RouterHealth" collided
                 (RTIXMLObject_addChild: "...::RouterHealth" already exists, WIS refused
                 to parse). type_ref="RouterHealth" still points at the real struct name
                 from the spliced types block; only this local registration alias
                 differs. The topic name itself MUST stay "RouterHealth", since it has to
                 match the actual DDS topic name router_main/PresenceMonitor.cxx
                 publishes on (default "RouterHealth", see PresenceMonitor.hpp). -->
            <register_type name="RouterHealthType" type_ref="RouterHealth" />
            <topic name="RouterHealth" register_type_ref="RouterHealthType" />
        </domain>
    </domain_library>

    <web_integration_service name="mesh_dashboard">
        <application name="MeshDashboardApp">
            <domain_participant name="MeshParticipant"
                    domain_ref="RouterAdminDomainLibrary::MeshWanDomain">
                <subscriber name="MeshSubscriber">
                    <data_reader name="RouterHealthReader" topic_ref="RouterHealth" />
                </subscriber>
            </domain_participant>
        </application>
    </web_integration_service>
</dds>
